         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Images from Nature\n\nThese images are copyright for Nature and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 1</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgNature\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgNature', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Mitochondrial DNA haplogroup composition of the 44 sewage samples with an average coverage of 10 or higher. (a) Mitochondrial DNA haplogroup composition of samples plotted at the site of the wastewater collection. Circle colors and colors of the pie charts correspond to specific haplogroups, while colors of the underscores indicate the four broad biogeographic ancestry categories. (b) Mitochondrial DNA haplogroup composition of samples using only the four broad biogeographic ancestry categories. Shared under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) license. © Dr. Anna Pipek Orsolya <i>et al</i> and Nature (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Dias/Díaz - Despite being a common surname, different people have used this surname without being connected over the past centuries. (<htcite1>)</li><li>Indigenous Abya Yala (America) - In this text, we study the Abya Yala (American) people as a unique family. (<htcite2>)</li><li>The Bantu People - This text presents the study on the Bantu and their expansion across the African continent. (<htcite3>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
